\textbf{Series: resistances add.} In a series string the same current $I$ passes through every resistor. The p.d.'s therefore add:
\[
V = IR_1 + IR_2 + \cdots = I\,(R_1+R_2+\cdots).
\]
Comparing with $V=IR_{\rm eqv}$ gives
\[
\boxed{R_{\rm eqv}=R_1+R_2+\cdots}\qquad\text{(series)}.
\]

