\end{center}

\textbf{Parallel: reciprocals add.} In a parallel bank every branch has the same p.d. $V$ across it, so each carries its own current $I_k=V/R_k$ and the branch currents add: $I=I_1+I_2+\cdots$. Dividing through by $V$:
\[
\frac{I}{V}=\frac{I_1}{V}+\frac{I_2}{V}+\cdots
\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
\frac{1}{R_{\rm eqv}}=\frac{1}{R_1}+\frac{1}{R_2}+\cdots,
\]
i.e.
\[
\boxed{\dfrac{1}{R_{\rm eqv}}=\dfrac{1}{R_1}+\dfrac{1}{R_2}+\cdots}\qquad\text{(parallel)}.
\]
For two resistors this simplifies to the familiar $R_{\rm eqv}=\dfrac{R_1R_2}{R_1+R_2}$.

